From adad2b26f4208d1beea360e8668a4eab263c5d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:26:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: round the encoder frame rate to the
 nearest integer

iris_venc_s_param() computes the frame rate as denominator / numerator
with integer division and stores it as whole frames per second, which is
what is then sent to the firmware as a Q16 value. Fractional rates are
therefore truncated: 30000/1001 (29.97) becomes 29, 24000/1001 (23.976)
becomes 23 and 60000/1001 becomes 59. The firmware's rate control sizes
each frame from bitrate / frame rate, so the stream comes out up to 4%
over the requested bitrate, and the clock and bandwidth estimates are
off by the same amount.

Round to the nearest integer, which is within 0.1% for all of the
common broadcast rates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHbRyvZ53xawh6pBdmacMe
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
index 54764c28a..2a2afa891 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
@@ -442,7 +442,8 @@ int iris_venc_s_param(struct iris_inst *inst, struct v4l2_streamparm *s_parm)
 			timeperframe->denominator = default_rate;
 	}
 
-	fps = timeperframe->denominator / timeperframe->numerator;
+	/* Round to nearest: 30000/1001 is 30 fps, not the 29 that truncation gives */
+	fps = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(timeperframe->denominator, timeperframe->numerator);
 	if (!fps)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
